      "commit_message": "test(passport): drive the generated dashboard in chromium (#77)\n\n* test(passport): drive the generated dashboard in chromium\n\nThe Python suite proves what goes into the page but never runs the ~980\nlines of authored JavaScript. tests_browser/ renders a synthetic log with\ncontrail.passport.render(), opens the file with pytest-playwright and\nexercises it: year, metric, cabin and reason controls, the ranking dialog\nincluding Escape, planned, unpriced and dateless flights, desktop and\nmobile viewports, and the #67 marker stacking and #72 departure fixes.\nAny page error, console error or non-local request fails the test.\n\nThe suite sits outside testpaths and its driver in a separate `browser`\nextra, so the Python matrix and coverage job stay browser independent.\nA new `ci / playwright` job installs Chromium only and uploads traces on\nfailure.\n\nFixes #62\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(passport): fail the call phase when the page misbehaves\n\npytest-playwright keeps a retain-on-failure trace only when the call\nphase fails. The page, console and network checks ran at fixture\nteardown, so a violation found only there discarded the trace that\nwould explain it. A pytest_runtest_call wrapper now raises them as the\ntest body ends; teardown still catches anything arriving later, without\nreporting the same finding twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "inspected_supporting_files": [
        "tests_browser/conftest.py"
      ]
    },
